<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ reports NZ$55.3 mln trade surplus in April.</title>
<headline>NZ reports NZ$55.3 mln trade surplus in April.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Monday released the following provisional statistics for New Zealand external merchandise trade for April.</p>
<p>(Figures are rounded, with revised-from data in brackets)</p>
<p>Monthly series:</p>
<p>		Apr 1997	    Mar 1997	     Apr 1996</p>
<p>Balance    +$55.3 million	  +$20.9 million (-$2.0)  +$122.6 million</p>
<p>Exports     $1.96 billion     $1.77 bln ($1.75)  $1.80 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $1.91 billion     $1.74 bln ($1.75)  $1.68 bln</p>
<p>		Yr-to-Apr 1997    Yr-to-Mar 1997     Yr-to-Apr 1996</p>
<p>Balance    -$541.1 million    -$473.8 million (-$498.2) -$997.7 bln</p>
<p>Exports     $20.93 bln	$20.77 bln ($20.75)  $20.54 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $21.47 bln	$21.24 bln ($21.25)  $21.54 bln</p>
<p>Trend series:</p>
<p>		Apr 1997	    Mar 1997	     Apr 1996</p>
<p>Balance    -$197.2 million    -$156.1 million (-$111.1) -$93.6 million</p>
<p>Exports     $1.65 billion  $1.67 bln ($1.66)     $1.71 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $1.85 billion  $1.83 bln ($1.77)     $1.80 bln</p>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters had on average expected a trade surplus of NZ$80.8 million for the month of April and a deficit of $487.7 million for the April year.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4) 473 4746</p>
</text>
